const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What concrete problems can you repair?',
    a: 'Cracks, surface scaling and spalling, chipped edges and nosings, and uneven sections. We repair and resurface concrete cracks and uneven surfaces to restore the space.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I know if my concrete needs repair or replacement?',
    a: 'Isolated cracks and surface wear on otherwise sound concrete are repair jobs. Cracks running the full width of a slab, sections that have heaved or sunk, or surface failure across most of the area point to replacement. We will tell you honestly which one you have.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will the repair match my existing concrete?',
    a: 'New repair material cures lighter and darkens as it weathers, so a fresh repair stands out at first and blends over a few seasons. Where the contrast would bother you, resurfacing a larger area gives a uniform look from day one.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a concrete repair last?',
    a: 'Done on sound concrete with proper prep, a repair lasts for years, and our work carries the same 2-year warranty as our new pours. Prep is where cheap repairs fail, and it is where we spend the time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you repair commercial concrete?',
    a: 'Yes. We handle commercial repair work including sidewalks, parking spaces and other structures for businesses across Toronto and the GTA.',
  },
];
---

